{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and motion (controllable) events. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear, safe states; move_forward is used for short progress; obstacle events trigger conservative, one-shot recovery turns (not full_rotate unless both sides are blocked). Recovery states only allow a single, safe turn action and return to exploration as soon as the path is clear. All uncontrollable events are handled in every state for determinism and safety.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect physical robot capabilities.",
    "Specification automaton binds sensor outcomes to safe, progress-oriented actions with conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
